      "answer": "```json\n{\"findings\": []}\n```\n\nI found no defect. I read the code by hand and did not run it, because this binding has no execution tool. This is not a repository verification, and no recipe was run.\n\n- **Loop invariant.** Every index below `lo` holds a value less than `x`, and every index at or above `hi` holds a value greater than or equal to `x`. The invariant holds at the start, with `lo=0` and `hi=a.length`.\n- **Midpoint.** `mid = lo + floor((hi-lo)/2)` always satisfies `lo <= mid < hi` while `lo < hi`, so `a[mid]` is always defined.\n- **Termination.** Both branches shrink the interval. `lo=mid+1` raises `lo`, and `hi=mid` lowers `hi` because `mid < hi`. The loop therefore ends.\n- **Result.** At exit `lo == hi`, so `lo` is the first index with `a[lo] >= x`, or `a.length` if there is none.\n- **Edge cases.**\n  - An empty array skips the loop and returns 0.\n  - Duplicate entries return the leftmost match, because equality takes the `hi=mid` branch.\n  - `-0` and `0` compare equal, so they do not change the result.\n  - Inputs are finite, so NaN cannot make a comparison unordered.\n- **Mutation.** The code only reads `a`, so the contract's no-mutation requirement holds.",
