      "answer": "```json\n{\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"line\": 2,\n      \"input\": {\n        \"root\": \"/a/b\",\n        \"target\": \"/a/bc\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"input\": {\n        \"status\": 2\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nBoth counterexamples come from reading the code against the stated contract. I did not run anything and I make no repository verification claim.\n\n- **Line 2:** `\"/a/bc\".startsWith(\"/a/b\")` is true. `/a/bc` is a sibling of `/a/b`, not the root or a descendant separated by `/`, so `inside` returns true where the contract requires false. The defect is the prefix test that ignores the path-segment boundary.\n- **Line 5:** `mayKeep` should accept only status 0, but `2 !== 1` is true. Status 2 means a recipe could not run, which the verification doctrine says must never be read as green. Any status other than 0 or 1 (2, -1, `null`) would also pass the same way, so this is one defect with status 2 as its counterexample.",
